WEBVTT

00:00.087 --> 00:30.032
The Donor of the Skin Transplant

00:00.507 --> 00:02.174
This is a story of Black Jack's beginning.

00:02.520 --> 00:07.233
There is a priceless story of
friendship under Doc's facial skin.

00:08.740 --> 00:10.447
You better stay out of this area.

00:10.767 --> 00:12.700
Especially outsiders like you, Kuro-chan.

00:12.813 --> 00:15.254
Is there any child who's willing
to donate skin for Kuroo-kun?

00:15.548 --> 00:16.908
You can use mine.

00:16.955 --> 00:19.357
Kuro-chan, I'll become a doctor.

00:19.756 --> 00:22.840
Nature and the environment are being
destroyed because of people's egoism.

00:23.207 --> 00:26.279
We need doctors who can restore nature on Earth!

00:26.454 --> 00:29.854
Black Jack, Today's Karte - The Donor of the Skin Transplant.

00:30.042 --> 00:36.665
I'm going to fly to where you are.

00:30.042 --> 00:36.665
kimi no moto e tonde yuku yo

00:37.000 --> 00:44.006
I know I can spread my wings when I want to see you.

00:37.000 --> 00:44.006
aitai toki tsubasa hiraku

00:44.591 --> 00:47.676
Nobody knows

00:44.591 --> 00:47.676
dara nimo wakaranai

00:48.095 --> 00:51.514
when a miracle might occur,

00:48.095 --> 00:51.514
kiseki wa itsu okiru?

00:51.515 --> 00:57.937
but it feels like my wish is finally coming true.

00:51.515 --> 00:57.937
nozomi wa kanaeraresou de

00:57.938 --> 01:04.735
Because there's only one place I want to go,

00:57.938 --> 01:04.735
mukau basho wa hitotsu shika nai kara

01:04.736 --> 01:07.988
iro asenai omoi yosete

01:04.736 --> 01:07.988
I gather my feelings whose colors never fade,

01:07.989 --> 01:11.534
and now it seems I'm dreaming.

01:07.989 --> 01:11.534
saa Dreaming now

01:12.119 --> 01:15.454
I'm living for your sake?

01:12.119 --> 01:15.454
kimi no tame ni iketeru

01:15.455 --> 01:18.624
I will be your strength,

01:15.455 --> 01:18.624
donna chikara nimo naru

01:18.917 --> 01:21.836
no matter how far apart we are.

01:18.917 --> 01:21.836
Far away Far away harukana

01:21.837 --> 01:25.631
So Freedom. So Freedom.

01:25.757 --> 01:29.218
I will send you

01:25.757 --> 01:29.218
kimi no tame no okurou

01:29.219 --> 01:32.471
the beautiful blossom of this flower.

01:29.219 --> 01:32.471
kirei ni saita hana wo

01:32.639 --> 01:35.558
So let's look for shooting stars.

01:32.639 --> 01:35.558
Shooting Star Shooting Star sagasou

01:35.559 --> 01:39.562
So Freedom. So Freedom.

02:12.637 --> 02:14.221
It's so,warm.

02:19.060 --> 02:19.759
His blood pressure?

02:19.978 --> 02:20.988
120 over 60.

02:21.313 --> 02:22.188
It's stable.

02:22.447 --> 02:24.565
Inject 1cc of Mioblock.

02:24.566 --> 02:25.524
OK.

02:33.157 --> 02:35.709
It's a huge blimp.

02:37.162 --> 02:39.538
Pinoco, thanks for waiting.

02:39.539 --> 02:40.456
Let's go have lunch.

02:40.457 --> 02:41.790
Aye-aye.

02:48.215 --> 02:49.757
It's so pretty!

02:49.758 --> 02:52.509
Yeah? You're from Japan?

02:52.510 --> 02:54.762
You've traveled a long way to come here.

02:55.347 --> 02:59.372
I've heard that Japan is very pretty
when the seasons change.

02:59.559 --> 03:04.188
The sky and sea are really pretty in this country too.

03:04.189 --> 03:06.482
W-Well, yeah.

03:14.658 --> 03:16.200
Delicious!

03:16.201 --> 03:20.955
It's wonderful to be able to eat lunch
at a place with a great view,

03:20.956 --> 03:24.124
This fish plate is just super.

03:24.125 --> 03:27.566
Pinoco, only talk or eat. Don't do both at the same time.

03:27.796 --> 03:30.172
But it's so delicious!

03:32.259 --> 03:33.974
Do you like the food?

03:34.221 --> 03:35.934
Yeah! It's the best!

03:35.994 --> 03:37.422
Thank you.

03:37.821 --> 03:39.742
These were caught locally, right?

03:39.801 --> 03:42.494
They'are all fresh and so delicious.

03:42.714 --> 03:44.561
N-No.

03:44.562 --> 03:48.190
Actually, all the fish came from elsewhere.

03:48.839 --> 03:50.499
What? Why?

03:50.944 --> 03:53.881
Even though you have such a pretty sea right there?

03:54.197 --> 03:59.513
We can't catch any fish here anymore.

04:05.750 --> 04:08.961
Originally "Where art thou, Friend?” by Tezuka Osamu

04:05.750 --> 04:08.961
The Donor of the Skin Transplant

04:20.348 --> 04:24.585
Grandpa, people say there's no fish here anymore.

04:24.978 --> 04:25.848
Yeah.

04:26.667 --> 04:30.316
This sea has died.

04:30.317 --> 04:31.567
Why?

04:31.568 --> 04:33.999
Why did this sea die?

04:36.531 --> 04:37.865
Because of that.

04:39.200 --> 04:42.934
That chemical plant was built two years ago.

04:43.121 --> 04:45.914
All the residents were opposed to it,

04:45.915 --> 04:52.254
but town officials, blinded by the money they
were offered, forced the agreement.

04:52.714 --> 04:58.969
Less than six months after the plant was built,
the residents' fears became a reality.

04:59.637 --> 05:00.846
As expected,

05:01.306 --> 05:03.743
the forest we were so proud of was destroyed,

05:04.476 --> 05:06.810
and the sea died off.

05:08.605 --> 05:14.238
They hold a demonstration to close
the plant almost every day.

05:15.195 --> 05:21.116
But it's nearly impossible to revert
everything back to normal.

05:21.826 --> 05:25.996
The price for destroying nature is huge.

05:29.042 --> 05:31.960
Give it back! Give it back! Give it back! Give it back!

05:31.961 --> 05:33.379
Give back our forest!

05:33.380 --> 05:34.838
Give back our sea!

05:34.839 --> 05:36.715
Close the plant immediately!

05:36.873 --> 05:40.180
Wow, so many people.

05:41.679 --> 05:42.638
Look!

05:55.858 --> 05:56.902
They fired at us!

05:56.903 --> 05:58.362
Run!

05:58.363 --> 06:00.322
Doc! My eyes hurt!

06:00.365 --> 06:01.407
It's tear gas.

06:01.408 --> 06:02.866
Don't inhale the gas.

06:02.867 --> 06:03.700
Yeah.

06:05.537 --> 06:06.245
Don't resist!

06:06.246 --> 06:08.080
Stop the demonstration immediately!

06:08.081 --> 06:09.957
Shut up, you puppet!

06:09.958 --> 06:11.166
Shut up!

06:11.918 --> 06:13.502
Hey! Don't use violence!

06:14.501 --> 06:16.338
Are you one of them?!

06:19.300 --> 06:21.051
Get off! Damn it!

06:24.931 --> 06:26.014
Get away from here quickly!

06:26.285 --> 06:29.667
You better stay out of this area.

06:29.978 --> 06:33.448
Especially outsiders like you, Kuro-chan.

06:33.857 --> 06:35.274
A-are you...

06:38.653 --> 06:40.803
Why does he know my name?

06:41.573 --> 06:43.615
And the way he said it...

06:44.951 --> 06:46.702
Bye, Kuro-chan.

06:48.329 --> 06:49.288
Takashi!

07:01.134 --> 07:02.038
Doc.

07:02.248 --> 07:02.961
Yes?

07:03.595 --> 07:06.847
Who's that Takashi you mentioned earlier?

07:07.432 --> 07:10.350
Takashi is my old friend.

07:10.536 --> 07:13.963
A priceless one at that.

07:28.119 --> 07:28.771
OK.

07:28.995 --> 07:31.830
We will now move on to grafting skin onto
the left cheek and the upper jaw.

07:31.831 --> 07:32.372
OK.

07:39.297 --> 07:40.839
No, that's too old.

07:40.840 --> 07:42.716
This skin is unusable.

07:42.942 --> 07:46.929
Doctor, this is the last stock of skin at this hospital.

07:46.930 --> 07:48.591
This is terrible.

07:49.015 --> 07:50.650
After coming this far...

07:51.267 --> 07:53.185
Everyone, we have a situation.

07:53.491 --> 07:55.687
We need new skin immediately.

07:55.688 --> 07:57.856
We need the freshest skin possible.

07:57.857 --> 07:58.941
OK.

07:58.942 --> 08:00.651
We will seek out everyone willing to donate his or her skin.

08:00.858 --> 08:02.319
He needs treatment quickly.

08:02.320 --> 08:02.986
I'll come too.

08:02.987 --> 08:03.704
OK.

08:04.938 --> 08:07.083
An old bomb detonated by accident.

08:07.408 --> 08:10.035
His mother is apparently in a vegetative state.

08:10.036 --> 08:11.411
That's terrible.

08:13.096 --> 08:15.098
I wonder how Kuroo-kun is doing.

08:15.289 --> 08:16.884
I hope he survives.

08:17.089 --> 08:18.255
Everyone gathered here,

08:19.225 --> 08:20.398
we have a favor to ask of you.

08:20.547 --> 08:24.925
Is there any child who's willing
to donate skin for Kuroo-kun?

08:25.062 --> 08:26.239
What?!

08:26.419 --> 08:27.279
Skin?

08:27.303 --> 08:29.132
You mean this? Skin?

08:29.389 --> 08:30.076
Yes!

08:30.306 --> 08:34.101
We can't work on Kuroo-kun without
a child's skin that is fresh.

08:34.811 --> 08:38.040
I can't give my daughter's skin.

08:38.356 --> 08:41.252
But it's your friend! Kuroo-kun, who needs the help!

08:41.901 --> 08:46.071
A child's skin has better regenenative ability,
giving us a better chance for success!

08:46.489 --> 08:47.775
We are running out of time.

08:48.032 --> 08:50.242
Somebody, please give your skin to Kuroo-kun!

08:50.493 --> 08:53.120
U-Um, my kid has something else planned now.

08:53.144 --> 08:53.744
Mine too.

08:53.910 --> 08:55.015
P-Please wait!

08:55.039 --> 08:55.956
Oh, my, it's this late already?

08:55.957 --> 08:57.207
Just a little!

08:57.208 --> 08:58.584
Only a little will do!

08:58.585 --> 08:59.543
Just...

09:02.295 --> 09:03.977
How terrible.

09:04.507 --> 09:06.883
Every single one left.

09:06.884 --> 09:09.386
Doctor, please use mine.

09:09.387 --> 09:14.648
Thank you, but there's a chance that
an adult's skin may not work.

09:15.184 --> 09:16.145
Right...

09:17.478 --> 09:18.979
You can use mine.

09:27.528 --> 09:29.906
W-What did you just say?

09:29.907 --> 09:31.450
Give him my skin.

09:32.368 --> 09:34.911
Y-You're willing to give him your skin?

09:34.912 --> 09:35.544
Yeah.

09:36.247 --> 09:38.832
Kuro-chan will be saved if I do, right?

09:38.833 --> 09:42.540
Kuro-chan let a me borrow his notebooks all the time.

09:42.795 --> 09:45.547
Thank you! Thank you so much!

09:45.548 --> 09:49.676
Doctor, his skin doesn't match Kuroo-kun's.

09:50.178 --> 09:53.644
If we use his skin, the difference
in color will be very apparent.

09:54.349 --> 09:55.724
That doesn't matter!

09:55.725 --> 09:56.975
We'll start the operation right now!

09:56.976 --> 09:57.649
OK!

09:59.937 --> 10:01.897
Leukocyte type matches.

10:01.898 --> 10:03.190
He has no known allergies either.

10:03.191 --> 10:05.150
Good. Let's take it from his chest.

10:05.151 --> 10:06.610
Commencing operation.

10:06.616 --> 10:06.983
Yes.

10:09.364 --> 10:11.281
We will detach subcutaneous tissue as well.

10:11.282 --> 10:11.823
OK.

10:14.285 --> 10:15.077
Hurry!

10:15.078 --> 10:16.662
We're racing against time!

10:26.021 --> 10:27.644
Good, good.

10:27.965 --> 10:29.363
Now, set it in place.

10:39.727 --> 10:41.288
Operation completed.

10:56.963 --> 10:57.963
Kuro-chan.

11:00.790 --> 11:03.664
Kuro-chan, I'm getting released before you.

11:06.254 --> 11:07.587
I've decided.

11:07.964 --> 11:10.005
When I grow up, I'll become a doctor.

11:10.508 --> 11:13.051
A doctor who will help people troubled by illness.

11:13.469 --> 11:17.136
Me, too. A doctor.

11:17.306 --> 11:19.388
Yeah? You'll be a doctor, too?

11:19.767 --> 11:21.643
Then we'll race to see who gets there first.

11:23.980 --> 11:25.567
Get well soon.

11:25.982 --> 11:28.191
Than-

11:28.192 --> 11:29.735
Than- you...

11:30.486 --> 11:32.446
I'll come see you again soon.

11:34.532 --> 11:36.283
Bye, Kuro-chan.

11:42.248 --> 11:44.434
Is Takashi your friend?

11:45.293 --> 11:45.970
Yeah.

11:46.294 --> 11:48.624
We walk from school together every day.

11:49.005 --> 11:53.561
Then we go out and catch tadpoles or insects together.

11:53.968 --> 11:55.135
I see.

11:55.261 --> 11:57.706
Don't let his gift go to waste.

11:57.810 --> 11:59.473
You must get well soon.

11:59.555 --> 12:00.849
I'll do my best.

12:00.892 --> 12:03.435
And I'll become a doctor like you,

12:03.710 --> 12:05.490
and pay him back.

12:08.650 --> 12:09.933
Kuroo-kun!

12:10.401 --> 12:11.651
Don't touch me!

12:13.783 --> 12:16.198
I-I can get up on my own.

12:41.140 --> 12:42.536
Look in the mirror.

12:45.311 --> 12:48.104
This skin is Takashi's?

12:48.105 --> 12:49.178
It is.

12:50.191 --> 12:51.191
Takashi!

12:51.275 --> 12:53.276
It's really his!

12:55.571 --> 12:57.864
After a painful rehabilitation that lasted several years,

12:58.282 --> 13:00.699
I was finally able to come back to school.

13:01.869 --> 13:05.247
But Takashi was no longer in Japan.

13:20.012 --> 13:22.935
What did you do after that?

13:23.724 --> 13:26.852
I went on to medical school to become a doctor.

13:27.520 --> 13:29.635
It was all to keep the promise with Takashi.

13:31.858 --> 13:34.609
Therefore, in this case...

13:37.530 --> 13:40.198
In a case like this...

13:45.037 --> 13:49.879
Kuroo, maybe you should have
plastic surgery on your face.

13:50.167 --> 13:53.628
Reconstructive technologies have come a
long way, and they have great skin too.

13:53.951 --> 13:59.342
Having a different colored skin grafted on your face
won't give your patients a good impression.

13:59.343 --> 14:00.302
Yup.

14:00.303 --> 14:03.009
There's no need for doctors to worry about
how the patients feel about us.

14:03.718 --> 14:08.894
Besides, this skin is from my priceless friend!

14:09.449 --> 14:11.062
U-uh, well...

14:11.063 --> 14:12.314
B-But...

14:17.486 --> 14:20.989
After my medical license was revoked,
I had many more opportunities to travel abroad.

14:21.365 --> 14:24.026
Each time, I searched for Takashi's whereabouts,

14:24.452 --> 14:27.746
but I could never find him.

14:30.291 --> 14:33.758
At last, I finally found Takashi.

14:34.795 --> 14:36.886
It's been over twenty years since then,

14:37.340 --> 14:38.798
but that's...

14:40.384 --> 14:41.837
Without a doubt, that's Takashi.

14:49.101 --> 14:49.917
Hello!

14:50.823 --> 14:51.695
It this Kuro-chan?

14:52.021 --> 14:52.631
Takashi!

14:53.209 --> 14:53.886
Is that you?

14:54.343 --> 14:54.895
Yeah.

14:55.608 --> 14:58.707
I never thought that you'd be in this country.

14:59.070 --> 15:01.529
Same goes for you! You're in this country!

15:02.281 --> 15:06.446
For years- no, decades- I've been looking for you!

15:06.869 --> 15:08.119
Really?

15:08.120 --> 15:09.079
I'm sorry about that.

15:09.080 --> 15:10.038
I want to see you!

15:10.039 --> 15:11.081
Where are you?

15:11.082 --> 15:12.031
I'll come out to you now.

15:12.708 --> 15:14.363
But the situation won't allow that.

15:16.045 --> 15:18.565
Because of the incident earlier today,
the authorities have their eyes on me.

15:18.881 --> 15:20.715
I can lose them,

15:21.300 --> 15:23.358
but you're probably a mark as well.

15:23.678 --> 15:24.415
What?

15:28.057 --> 15:28.966
That must be them.

15:29.809 --> 15:31.492
They're after me.

15:31.852 --> 15:33.687
They learned that you know me,

15:33.944 --> 15:35.273
so they're waiting for you to come in contact with me.

15:35.815 --> 15:37.941
Takashi, how did you get involved in—

15:37.942 --> 15:40.346
Do you still want to see me?

15:40.611 --> 15:41.564
Of course I do!

15:43.322 --> 15:44.198
All right,

15:44.573 --> 15:46.408
then let's do this.

15:47.493 --> 15:49.369
We'll be out for a bit.

15:49.370 --> 15:50.870
Have a safe walk.

15:56.293 --> 15:58.159
They're really following us.

15:58.462 --> 16:00.005
Do what we talked about.

16:00.006 --> 16:00.964
Leave it to me!

16:04.677 --> 16:05.260
Go after the black one!

16:05.261 --> 16:05.885
Yeah!

16:16.147 --> 16:17.147
Hey! This way!

16:27.950 --> 16:29.271
Welcome.

16:29.577 --> 16:32.203
Hey! Good work again today!

16:33.205 --> 16:34.164
Come on over.

16:34.358 --> 16:35.415
Let's drink together.

16:35.416 --> 16:36.583
Yeah, yeah!

16:36.584 --> 16:37.792
Let's drink!

16:37.793 --> 16:41.004
Well, we're still on duty...

16:41.005 --> 16:42.297
S-So, uh...

16:42.298 --> 16:43.965
What?

16:43.966 --> 16:47.177
You dare refuse my offer?!

16:47.178 --> 16:47.877
Huh?

16:48.137 --> 16:50.388
W-Well, that's not...

16:50.538 --> 16:52.640
Then let's drink!

16:52.641 --> 16:54.267
We'll have fun together.

16:54.268 --> 16:55.560
B-But...

16:55.561 --> 16:58.480
Can't you hear? I said, "Let's drink!”

16:58.481 --> 17:00.774
B-But, it's...

17:02.485 --> 17:04.152
Doc, did it work?

17:04.904 --> 17:06.693
I asked everyone here for a huge favor.

17:06.906 --> 17:08.807
Crap! They're getting away!

17:09.075 --> 17:11.618
I'm not letting you go until you accept my offer!

17:13.079 --> 17:14.496
They got away!

17:14.497 --> 17:15.716
Damn!

17:18.226 --> 17:18.779
Yes.

17:20.628 --> 17:21.795
He did?

17:34.809 --> 17:37.160
This is just about the spot.

17:39.814 --> 17:43.024
But I can't find anyone like him.

17:49.907 --> 17:50.865
Takashi!

17:53.119 --> 17:54.410
Kuro-chan.

17:55.788 --> 17:58.589
I heard rumors that you became a doctor.

17:58.999 --> 18:04.295
We made a promise that we'd both become doctors.

18:04.296 --> 18:07.185
Takashi, what do you do now?

18:07.967 --> 18:09.641
Why are the police after you?

18:11.053 --> 18:13.197
I became a doctor too.

18:14.348 --> 18:15.887
There are many types of doctors.

18:16.267 --> 18:18.774
Look at the scenery after dark.

18:19.436 --> 18:20.647
Isn't it pretty?

18:21.105 --> 18:23.753
But it's all on the surface.

18:24.191 --> 18:29.936
The moon-lit sea is already dead because of that plant.

18:30.406 --> 18:31.643
It's not just here.

18:32.199 --> 18:36.985
Nature and the environment are being destroyed
because of people's egoism.

18:38.080 --> 18:39.831
Global climate changes,

18:40.416 --> 18:41.777
destruction of the ozone layer,

18:42.418 --> 18:44.002
diminishing tropical rainforests:

18:44.003 --> 18:45.253
there are countless issues.

18:46.088 --> 18:46.940
Yes.

18:47.173 --> 18:50.967
What I'm trying to cure is the Earth.

18:51.927 --> 18:53.364
The Earth is alive!

18:53.929 --> 18:59.472
But there are many bacteria who are trying
to get the Earth sick and kill it.

18:59.810 --> 19:03.980
At this rate, the situation will get progressively
worse, and eventually...

19:07.541 --> 19:10.744
We need doctors who can restore nature on Earth!

19:11.238 --> 19:15.742
So we planned to bomb that plant
in order to stop the pollution!

19:17.620 --> 19:20.038
It will happen soon.

19:20.039 --> 19:21.122
What?!

19:21.123 --> 19:23.294
You extract cancer cells out of
your patients too, don't you?

19:23.667 --> 19:26.628
The cancer cells on Earth must be eliminated!

19:26.629 --> 19:28.880
Those two topics are completely different!

19:28.881 --> 19:30.298
And there's the possibility of human casualties too!

19:30.299 --> 19:31.507
Isn't there any other way?

19:31.698 --> 19:34.302
They won't see it unless we go that far!

19:39.725 --> 19:42.769
Doc! There are so many police cars here!

19:42.770 --> 19:44.479
Takashi, what do we do?

19:44.855 --> 19:45.703
It's OK.

19:45.981 --> 19:48.233
I'll never get caught.

19:48.234 --> 19:49.871
Surround the Ferris wheel!

20:05.084 --> 20:07.001
Kuro-chan, thank you.

20:08.545 --> 20:09.313
Takashi!

20:09.968 --> 20:11.973
I'm glad I could see you.

20:15.511 --> 20:16.439
Goodbye.

20:23.769 --> 20:25.311
He jumped into the sea!

20:25.312 --> 20:26.098
Go after him!

20:26.427 --> 20:29.327
But I can't swim...

20:29.920 --> 20:30.987
You wimp!

20:31.087 --> 20:32.671
After him!

20:39.034 --> 20:41.869
Takashi disappeared into the darkness of the sea.

20:44.999 --> 20:49.252
I never got to see Takashi after that.

20:58.808 --> 21:00.096
Oh, Doc!

21:00.097 --> 21:04.058
The coffee is ready, so I was just about to come get you.

21:04.188 --> 21:06.269
It's my special blend.

21:06.270 --> 21:09.480
I'd say it's ten times more delicious than the one at Tom's.

21:10.149 --> 21:10.565
Really?

21:11.108 --> 21:13.234
Yes, it smells delicious.

21:13.235 --> 21:16.517
Both the smell and taste are great.

21:17.197 --> 21:23.116
A nature conservationist group had a sit in
at a chemical plant earlier today.

21:23.370 --> 21:26.334
A military group was deployed,
and the situation has been resolved.

21:26.623 --> 21:28.916
There were casualties among the
conservationist group as a result.

21:29.835 --> 21:33.212
It's the plant we saw.
There is a report that one of them is Japanese,

21:33.308 --> 21:36.174
but that has not yet been confirmed.

21:36.175 --> 21:40.887
The Japanese embassy and Ministry of
Foreign Affairs are working together

21:40.888 --> 21:43.960
to account for all Japanese residents there.

21:42.341 --> 21:43.081
Takashi!

21:48.082 --> 21:49.124
Doc...

22:01.283 --> 22:04.994
Takashi, I'll take good care of this skin.

22:10.042 --> 22:11.667
The Earth is alive.

22:12.711 --> 22:16.798
We need doctors who can restore nature on Earth!

22:18.592 --> 22:19.634
Kuro-chan...

22:24.098 --> 22:29.210
As you look at the ground uncertainly,

22:24.098 --> 22:29.210
tamerai gachi no fuseta hitomi

22:29.211 --> 22:34.507
I gently pull your hair closer to me.

22:29.211 --> 22:34.507
kono te ga sono kami hikiyoseteta

22:35.138 --> 22:41.639
You didn't speak, but only sighed,

22:35.138 --> 22:41.639
nani mo iezu ni kobore ochita tameiki

22:41.640 --> 22:46.102
and wet my chest with your tears.

22:41.640 --> 22:46.102
namida ga mune wo nurashita

22:46.103 --> 22:51.357
You longed to hear it, even if it was a lie.

22:46.103 --> 22:51.357
use demo ii... to kitto nozonde ita

22:51.358 --> 22:56.112
But I couldn't give you the answer you wanted.

22:51.358 --> 22:56.112
kimi no kimochi ni kotae kirezu

22:56.113 --> 23:04.537
If I gave you that answer, despite my cowardice,

22:56.113 --> 23:04.537
okubyou na boku ga moshi sono toki kotaetetara mada

23:04.538 --> 23:08.124
would we still be together?

23:04.538 --> 23:08.124
tsuzuiteita noka?

23:08.125 --> 23:13.421
That irregular breath my body was accustomed to,

23:08.125 --> 23:13.421
karada ga oboeta fukisoku na breath

23:13.425 --> 23:18.885
I want to feel it one more time.

23:13.425 --> 23:18.885
mou ichido subete de kanjitai

23:18.886 --> 23:24.390
The breath of surprise when I lost everything.

23:18.886 --> 23:24.390
subete wo nakushita fuyoui na breath

23:24.391 --> 23:33.566
And the pain that binds me every time I feel regret.

23:24.391 --> 23:33.566
kuyamu tabi mata sono itami ga shimetsukeru

23:45.056 --> 24:14.998
Pinoco's School Entrance Exam Journal

23:45.463 --> 23:46.756
Pinoco makes a huge hassle!

23:46.823 --> 23:48.463
I get in the middle of a school entrance exam!

23:48.583 --> 23:49.750
Just watch, Doc.

23:49.850 --> 23:52.030
I'll work hard and get accepted!

23:52.123 --> 23:53.723
I want to go to school.

23:53.890 --> 23:55.910
Can't Pinoco-chan make that wish?

23:56.150 --> 23:56.710
What's your point?

23:57.070 --> 23:59.048
I see your situation.

23:59.241 --> 24:01.188
So, does she excel academically?

24:01.268 --> 24:03.641
In anything, you must start at the basics.

24:03.735 --> 24:05.601
I don't have enough fingers.

24:05.684 --> 24:06.191
Start!

24:08.930 --> 24:10.930
But Pinoco is different from regular people.

24:11.230 --> 24:14.575
Black Jack, Next Karte - Pinoco's School Entrance Exam Journal.

24:16.139 --> 24:17.889
Karte NG...

24:18.610 --> 24:19.618
Doc...
